[{"id":112313,"sender_id":25,"sender_full_name":"David_Corfield","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7d52fbe20c8ac05886a296e9ee2159b1?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/random.20surface/near/112313\">#1</a> Looks interesting</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Darrick Lee, Harald Oberhauser, <em>Random Surfaces and Higher Algebra</em> [<a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.08366\">arXiv:2311.08366</a>].</li>\n</ul>\n<p>We don’t yet have a ‘random surface’ entry, a concept used by Polyakov in <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Polyakov+gauge-string+duality+--+references#Polyakov08\">string theory</a>.</p>","timestamp":1700206891,"subject":"random surface","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":112316,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/random.20surface/near/112316\">#2</a> Maybe an entry on random surfaces would be worthwhile (your link on “string theory” was meant to point to <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Polyakov+gauge-string+duality+--+references#Polyakov08\">Polyakov 2008</a>).</p>\n<p>But first and foremost that article should be cited at <em><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/higher%20parallel%20transport\">higher parallel transport</a></em>. Have now added it <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/higher+parallel+transport#LeeOberhauser23\">there</a>.</p>","timestamp":1700219020,"subject":"random surface","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]}]